# CODEOWNERS
#
# Purpose:
# This file defines the owners responsible for reviewing changes
# to specific files or directories in this repository.
#
# How it works:
# - Each rule maps a file/directory pattern to one or more owners.
# - Owners can be individual GitHub users or GitHub teams.
# - When a Pull Request changes a matching file, GitHub automatically
#   requests a review from the specified owner(s).
# - If branch protection requires CODEOWNER approval, the PR cannot
#   be merged until the required owner approves it.
#
# Syntax:
# <file/directory pattern> <owner>
#
# Examples:
# /src/Backend/ @backend-team
# /src/Frontend/ @frontend-team
#
# Note:
# This file should be named exactly "CODEOWNERS" (without .md or .txt)
# and is typically located under .github/CODEOWNERS.

